          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures beginning at age 17. Seizures currently occur approximately four times per week. The epilepsy is drug-resistant. The etiology is genetic, due to a causative STXBP1 variant, c.902A>G. Brain MRI demonstrates nonspecific white matter changes.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medications:\n- Valproate\n- Levetiracetam\n- Lacosamide\n- Oxcarbazepine\n\nSeizure Burden:\nApproximately four generalized tonic-clonic seizures per week despite the current antiseizure medication regimen.\n\nAssessment:\nDrug-resistant generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures, with onset at age 17 and a genetic etiology related to STXBP1 c.902A>G. MRI shows nonspecific white matter changes.\n\nPlan:\nContinue management on the current antiseizure medication regimen, with ongoing assessment of seizure burden and drug-resistant epilepsy.",
